---
import {ArrowRight,Mail} from 'lucide-react';
import {guideImages} from '../data/refinedImages';
import ReadingHeader from './ReadingHeader.astro';
import PageContents from './PageContents.astro';
const visual=guideImages['prototype-vs-small-batch-cnc'];
const steps=[{name:'Validate',text:'Check fit, function or appearance with a first sample.',href:'#section-1'},{name:'Approve',text:'Lock the drawing, material and finish with agreed inspection.',href:'#section-2'},{name:'Repeat',text:'Carry the approved specification into controlled production.',href:'#section-3'}];
const suppliers=[{title:'Same specification',text:'Make sure each quote uses the same drawing revision, material and finish.'},{title:'What is included',text:'Check setup, inspection records, packaging and delivery basis are stated.'},{title:'Exclusions or substitutions',text:'Confirm that any exclusions or substitutions are clear.'},{title:'Changes and repeat orders',text:'Ask how changes, nonconforming parts and repeat orders will be handled.'}];
const contents=[...steps.map(step=>({id:step.href.slice(1),label:step.name})),{id:'section-4',label:'Compare suppliers'},{id:'section-5',label:'Next batch RFQ'}];
---
<article class="approval-guide reading-page">
 <ReadingHeader title="CNC prototypes and small-batch production" description="A prototype helps you check the design before ordering more parts. For a repeat batch, use the approved drawing revision and confirm the material and finish. You also need an agreed inspection plan and delivery terms." breadcrumbs={[{label:'Resources',href:'/resources/'},{label:'Production planning'}]}/>
 <PageContents entries={contents}/>
 <div class="ag-wrap ag-stage-notes reading-overview">{steps.map(step=><p><strong>{step.name}.</strong> {step.text}</p>)}</div>
 <figure class="ag-wrap reading-figure ag-overview-figure" data-image-origin="AI-generated"><img src={visual.image} srcset={visual.srcset} sizes="(max-width:760px) 90vw, 1140px" width="1536" height="1024" alt={visual.alt} loading="lazy"/><figcaption>AI-generated illustration — not an LZZ order or production record.</figcaption></figure>
 <section class="ag-wrap ag-chapter reading-section" id="section-1"><div class="ag-intro"><span class="ag-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><h2>Validate<br/>the first sample</h2><p>Agree what the sample must prove: assembly fit, a critical interface, operation or appearance. Define the checks needed for sample acceptance before moving to a repeat order.</p></div></div><dl class="ag-review"><div><dt>Drawing questions</dt><dd>Use the sample to identify design questions related to fit, function or appearance.</dd></div><div><dt>Workholding and access</dt><dd>Review workholding and tool access while confirming the design.</dd></div><div><dt>Material, finish and acceptance</dt><dd>Check the specified grade, condition and final appearance. Define fit, function and sample acceptance checks. Confirm the prototype price and schedule for the specific part.</dd></div></dl></section>
 <section class="ag-band reading-section" id="section-2"><div class="ag-wrap ag-chapter ag-approval"><div class="ag-intro"><span class="ag-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><h2>Approve what<br/>will repeat</h2><p>For a repeat order, release one controlled drawing revision and carry the approved material and finish into the quotation. Agree the acceptance plan and the documents to accompany delivery.</p></div></div><div><div class="ag-columns"><div><h4>Specification to carry forward</h4><ul><li>Agree revision approval and how changed features are identified.</li><li>Confirm material documents and the finish standard, including masking and dimensions after treatment.</li><li>Retain the approved specification unless a change is agreed.</li></ul></div><div><h4>Evidence to agree</h4><ul><li>Define batch sampling and critical-feature records.</li><li>Confirm the measurement method, instrument evidence and available report format.</li><li>Agree the acceptance plan and delivery documents.</li></ul></div></div></div><p class="ag-change">If the drawing changes, pause and confirm the impact. The old sample may no longer represent the new revision.</p></div></section>
 <section class="ag-wrap ag-chapter ag-repeat reading-section" id="section-3"><div class="ag-intro"><span class="ag-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><h2>Plan the<br/>repeat order</h2><p>Confirm the setup and machining sequence for the released revision, including critical datums, and whether the route changes with quantity. Request a new quote for the batch quantity and price, and confirm the production slot.</p><p><strong>There is no fixed quantity threshold for an economical small batch.</strong><br/>Economics depend on the part geometry and its setup.</p></div></div><div class="ag-planning"><dl><div><dt>Minimum order</dt><dd>1 piece</dd></div><div><dt>Production lead time</dt><dd>7–14 business days</dd></div></dl><p>after drawing and order confirmation, including surface finishing.</p><p>Shipping time is additional.</p><p>Share the part, quantity and required arrival date so we can quote price and delivery arrangements.</p></div></section>
 <section class="ag-wrap ag-suppliers reading-section" id="section-4"><h2>Compare suppliers before committing</h2><p>Compare the quoted scope, not headline unit price alone. Use the same drawing revision, material and finish, and check the following points with each supplier.</p><div>{suppliers.map(s=><section><h3>{s.title}</h3><p>{s.text}</p></section>)}</div></section>
 <section class="ag-wrap ag-related reading-related" aria-labelledby="article-examples-title"><div><h2 id="article-examples-title">Related part examples</h2><p>The engine-cover example covers prototype clearances; the enclosure example covers thin walls and batch inspection.</p></div><div><a href="/products/custom-billet-aluminum-engine-cover-manufacturer-and-automotive-prototype-supplier/">Billet aluminum engine covers <ArrowRight size={18}/></a><a href="/products/precision-small-batch-cnc-milling-manufacturer-for-complex-aluminum-enclosures/">Small-batch aluminum enclosures <ArrowRight size={18}/></a></div></section>
 <nav class="ag-wrap ag-bottom" aria-label="Related resources"><a class="ag-link" href="/resources/">Back to Resources</a><a class="ag-link" href="/resources/how-we-work/">Ordering guide <ArrowRight size={18}/></a></nav>
 <section class="ag-wrap ag-rfq reading-closing" id="section-5"><h2>What to include in your next batch RFQ</h2><p>Share the drawing, first-order quantity, expected repeat pattern and required arrival date. Identify critical dimensions and records, then confirm price, production slot, inspection evidence, finish, packing and shipping terms for that order. The <a href="/resources/how-we-work/">ordering guide</a> explains the information to agree before shipment.</p><div class="ag-actions"><a class="ag-button" href="/quote/">Prepare RFQ email</a><a class="ag-link" href="mailto:roger@lzz-cnc.com"><Mail size={18}/>roger@lzz-cnc.com</a></div></section>
</article>
<style>
